#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Kan-chan: the KantanOS companion.

A character who lives on the PC: chat by talking or typing, she keeps notes about you (in a
database in your home folder, all visible and editable in "What I remember"), brings things
up, helps with everyday things like what to cook, and hands PC problems to the KantanOS
Helper. Her voice, ears, name and AI settings are shared with the Helper. If you let her, she
can see through the webcam while her window is open: she recognises the people you introduce
to her (on this PC; no photos are kept) and notices things like a new haircut. She can also
notice which games you play and which shows you watch (kanchan-notice, each switched on
separately in "What I remember") and ask how they're going.

  kanchan            open her window
  kanchan --enable   put her in the app menu (Welcome does this), then open
  kanchan --disable  take her out of the app menu again (notes are kept)
  kanchan --check-in the once-a-day hello at login (only when "Say hello each day" is on)
  kanchan --listen   open her window (or bring it forward) and start listening; again to stop
                     (Meta+K from anywhere)

Email and calendar (her window → "Email and calendar…"): she reads emails aloud, replies, writes
to people and bins emails through Thunderbird (mail.py), always asking first, and reminds the
person about appointments from their own calendars (agenda.py, kanchan-remind).
"""
